{
  "id": "kpk1-l04-b3",
  "section": {
    "letter": "B",
    "heading": "Koniugacja -ę, -isz/-ysz",
    "meaning": {
      "en": "Verbs in -ę, -isz and -ysz"
    },
    "strands": [
      "G"
    ]
  },
  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l04-b3-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l04-b3-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "Słyszeć: to hear"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "*Słyszeć* has *sz* before its ending, so it goes like *uczyć się*: *słyszę*, *słyszysz*, *słyszy*, *słyszymy*, *słyszycie*, *słyszą*. *Nie słyszę, proszę powtórzyć* is \"I can't hear, please say it again\"."
      },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "słyszeć",
        "meaning": {
          "en": "to hear"
        },
        "forms": {
          "ja": "słyszę",
          "ty": "słyszysz",
          "on": "słyszy",
          "my": "słyszymy",
          "wy": "słyszycie",
          "oni": "słyszą"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l04-b3-t02",
      "before": "kpk1-l04-b3-e06",
      "title": {
        "en": "Robić: an extra i"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "After *b*, *p*, *w*, *f*, *m* and *n*, the forms for *ja* and *oni* have an extra *i*, as in *mówię* and *mówią*: *robię*, *robią*, but *robisz*, *robi*. *Lubić*, to like, goes the same way: *lubię*, *lubisz*. *Co robisz?* asks a friend \"what are you doing?\"."
      },
      "conjugation": {
        "verb": "robić",
        "meaning": {
          "en": "to do, to make"
        },
        "forms": {
          "ja": "robię",
          "ty": "robisz",
          "on": "robi",
          "my": "robimy",
          "wy": "robicie",
          "oni": "robią"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
